112:Definition BB5 := 47176870%N.
3:  The statement (see `BB5_value_statement`) and the definitions are quite transparent, the only prerequisite is to know what Turing machine are.
119:Definition BB5_value_statement :=
100:(** `HaltsAtPlusOne tm n st` holds if Turing machine `tm` halts at configuration `st` after `n` steps.
102:  Note: Coq-BB5 'HaltsAt' definition (see TM.v) is off by one compared to Radò's definition which is why we have to use 'HaltsAtPlusOne'
105:Inductive HaltsAtPlusOne(tm:TM): nat->ExecState->Prop :=
106:| HaltsAtPlusOne_intro n st:
108:  HaltsAtPlusOne tm (S n) st.
120:  (forall tm n0, HaltsAtPlusOne Σ tm n0 (InitES Σ Σ0) -> n0 <= N.to_nat BB5) /\
121:  (exists tm, HaltsAtPlusOne Σ tm (N.to_nat BB5) (InitES Σ Σ0)).
